All 12 trials scored 0 on dev and 0 on training success. Because the mask and the logits are both in action space, they always share a frame. So any net that feeds the obs under all 8 symmetries already covers every dihedral obs-to-action relation. Taken together, r1c3, r2c1 and r2c3 make a dihedral frame mismatch unlikely, whether the action order is type-major or type-minor. Each was one seed and each summed four output layouts, which may have diluted the signal. No net has yet tested the 8 obs views with only the identity layout, so candidate 1 does that. Not ruled out yet:
- a non-dihedral spatial remap, such as a roll or shuffle;
- DONE placed at index 0;
- per-channel offsets that per-cell LayerNorm cannot remove;
- the obs memory read as channels-last;
- an arbitrary scramble.
